// SECOND DRAFT (M5): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
EXTERNAL flag(name)
Skögul hands you a grey feather, curled at the tip and bound to a handle of bone.
"Some of the fallen are only mostly dead." # speaker: skogul
"They come up the path with the rest, because nobody tells them not to. Hold this under the nose. If it stirs, stamp RETURN, and they go home." # speaker: skogul
The feather is so light you can barely feel it in your hand.
"It costs daylight. Save it for the ones whose breath fogs in the cold, not every corpse that looks sleepy." # speaker: skogul
{ flag("asked_about_lies"):
  "You asked about liars on your first day. The mostly dead lie too. They think they're dreaming, so they say whatever sounds best." # speaker: skogul
}
* ["How do they get back?"]
  "Badly. They wake in a ditch with a headache and a story nobody believes." # speaker: skogul
  "Most of them learn to stay out of battles after that. Most." # speaker: skogul
* ["Has anyone ever come back twice?"]
  Skögul looks down the queue for a long moment, as if she's counting something.
  "One. You'll meet him." # speaker: skogul
  # fx: flag asked_twice
  She doesn't say whether that's a warning.
- The queue is longer today. Somewhere near the back, someone is humming a drinking song, badly, and apologising to the people around him.
-> END
